WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.488
- My eyelashes look like whiskers.

00:00:02.488 --> 00:00:04.439
I would say I'm lookin' like I'm about

00:00:04.439 --> 00:00:06.823
to go out for an audition
to Cats right now.

00:00:06.823 --> 00:00:10.654
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:10.654 --> 00:00:12.259
So we've been dating almost four years

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:15.277
and we also have been living
together for two years.

00:00:15.277 --> 00:00:17.437
- We've been dating for a year and a half.

00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:18.760
We do not live together.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.175
- To me, she seems like the
quintessential morning person.

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:22.289
- I hate mornings.

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:25.454
I have like a 6:50 alarm, a 6:55 alarm,

00:00:25.454 --> 00:00:27.219
and a 7:02 alarm.

00:00:27.219 --> 00:00:29.889
- I go to a boot camp
class and then I go back

00:00:29.889 --> 00:00:31.027
to the townhouse.

00:00:31.027 --> 00:00:33.674
- Uh, okay, but you're
forgetting a couple things.

00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:35.624
I've caught you several times sitting

00:00:35.624 --> 00:00:37.598
in your car eating chips.

00:00:37.598 --> 00:00:39.386
I think she does it enough
that she should consider

00:00:39.386 --> 00:00:40.988
that part of her schedule.

00:00:40.988 --> 00:00:44.076
- And then I put a spoonful
of coconut oil in my mouth.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.353
- It doesn't do anything!

00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:47.536
- No, it does, it's called oil pulling.

00:00:47.536 --> 00:00:49.790
It's good for teeth whitening
and battling cavities

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.295
and general --
- [Man] You have more cavities

00:00:51.295 --> 00:00:52.644
than I have, though.

00:00:52.644 --> 00:00:54.339
- Well, I just started doing this.

00:00:54.339 --> 00:00:55.175
- There you go.

00:00:55.175 --> 00:00:56.730
- I like keeping things simple and easy.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.190
- She's like the fast food
drive-thru method of makeup.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:00.933
- Yeah.

00:01:00.933 --> 00:01:02.907
- Convenience, consistency.

00:01:02.907 --> 00:01:04.494
- I don't do my makeup
until I get to work.

00:01:05.962 --> 00:01:06.746
- Nice!

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:13.949
- I think I got the
shit end of the bargain.

00:01:13.949 --> 00:01:16.087
Your morning is just harder in every way.

00:01:21.339 --> 00:01:23.383
I don't know how I'm
gonna, I may just die.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.239
(fast-paced percussive music)

00:01:25.239 --> 00:01:27.236
- I don't really know why
I would use coconut oil.

00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:29.581
I think I have pretty
good oral hygiene already.

00:01:29.581 --> 00:01:32.809
- I just pulled in to my 6:10 a.m. class.

00:01:32.809 --> 00:01:34.746
(fast-paced electronic music)

00:01:34.746 --> 00:01:36.156
It wasn't as bad as I thought it would be.

00:01:36.156 --> 00:01:38.080
It was like I was too tired to feel tired,

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.148
if that makes any sense.

00:01:39.148 --> 00:01:40.657
- I didn't look up how much coconut oil

00:01:40.657 --> 00:01:41.818
I was supposed to put in my mouth,

00:01:41.818 --> 00:01:43.311
but here we go, this
is what it looks like.

00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:45.092
That looks really, really gross.

00:01:46.862 --> 00:01:48.523
(mumbles)

00:01:48.523 --> 00:01:51.681
- Got my bag of chips, soda.

00:01:51.681 --> 00:01:53.817
It's crazy to me to think
that eating junk food

00:01:53.817 --> 00:01:56.859
right after working out is
like part of her routine,

00:01:56.859 --> 00:01:58.333
but it's kinda satisfying.

00:02:00.962 --> 00:02:04.236
So Jen left me a little surprise: makeup.

00:02:04.236 --> 00:02:06.604
Blush, am I supposed to wet this?

00:02:06.604 --> 00:02:08.090
This is something I never even noticed,

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:10.180
so I don't really know what
I'm trying to replicate here.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:10.880
Okay.

00:02:12.163 --> 00:02:13.742
Holy shit, that's a lot.

00:02:15.506 --> 00:02:17.155
You do like a dab dab dab.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.556
I look like a Bond villain right now.

00:02:21.556 --> 00:02:23.821
- It didn't taste that
bad, kinda liked it.

00:02:23.821 --> 00:02:25.562
- Okay, now we've got liner.

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:27.536
She put "above lashes."

00:02:27.536 --> 00:02:29.533
(bleep) was I supposed to?

00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:31.762
- I'm gonna brush my teeth
because it was really sweet.

00:02:31.762 --> 00:02:33.480
My mom taught me that if
you eat anything sugar,

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.827
you've gotta brush your teeth.

00:02:34.827 --> 00:02:37.682
- So I missed, where's like
the magic makeup eraser?

00:02:37.682 --> 00:02:38.983
That's what I need right now.

00:02:38.983 --> 00:02:41.094
(upbeat country music)

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.648
- I was surprised with
how thick coconut oil is.

00:02:43.648 --> 00:02:46.504
- It gets thicker 'cause it's
like takin' up the toxins

00:02:46.504 --> 00:02:47.966
from your mouth.
- [Man] Really?

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:49.364
- [Woman] Yeah!
- [Man] Okay, I had no idea

00:02:49.364 --> 00:02:50.472
what I was doing with that thing.

00:02:50.472 --> 00:02:51.317
It was delicious, though.

00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:53.493
- When I first saw him,
I couldn't stop laughing.

00:02:53.493 --> 00:02:55.621
- I just felt ashamed and embarrassed

00:02:55.621 --> 00:02:56.782
walking out of the bathroom.

00:02:56.782 --> 00:02:57.517
She was waiting

00:02:57.517 --> 00:02:58.586
for me.
- [Woman] Steve was like,

00:02:58.586 --> 00:02:59.328
"Do not look at me."

00:02:59.328 --> 00:03:00.597
- I tried to write an e-mail for work

00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.061
and it just was like, this is gibberish.

00:03:02.061 --> 00:03:05.776
And soon I had to take
a nap, at like 9:15.

00:03:05.776 --> 00:03:07.726
- The amount of time
I had to do everything

00:03:07.726 --> 00:03:08.810
was really satisfying.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.268
- I think that there's
definitely something

00:03:10.268 --> 00:03:11.705
I've learned from this, where there's like

00:03:11.705 --> 00:03:13.109
other good things you can extract

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:14.159
from other people's routines.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:16.239
Like, for instance, the coconut
oil seems like a good thing.

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:18.778
- That is a huge
concession, because he hated

00:03:18.778 --> 00:03:20.018
that coconut oil.

00:03:20.018 --> 00:03:21.612
- Well, I hate it 'cause
I can't talk to Sophia

00:03:21.612 --> 00:03:23.306
so here's the solution:
We do it at the same time.

00:03:23.306 --> 00:03:25.071
- It's definitely a weird
feeling to just like

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.601
start eating junk food
immediately after like having

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:29.436
one of the hardest workouts of your life.

00:03:29.436 --> 00:03:31.627
But it was also really satisfying too.

